{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Two by two they came.</b> The verse is precise in saying <b>they came</b>, for they were not made to be gathered after — rather they came of themselves. And it says <b>two two</b> concerning every detail of those that came, thereby including clean animals and birds, even though He had commanded seven of them. According to what I explained above, the verse is precisely understood: for what is needed for the survival of the species is only two, and those HaShem brought to the ark, and it received them. But the supplement of the seven — Noah himself took the trouble to take them, as HaShem commanded him: ״תִּקַּח לְךָ״ — since it is not for the survival of the species, he must exert himself on his own, and they would not impose upon him from heaven. And so you will find further in another verse (Genesis 7:15): ״וַיָּבֹאוּ אֶל נֹחַ אֶל הַתֵּבָה שְׁנַיִם שְׁנַיִם״ — meaning: what came of themselves were two by two."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:01.914010505Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}